{"parentUuid":"bf74a737-a435-4656-af31-d99096083684","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"02289edc-3f1c-4d2c-8649-2b62a8e61cf4","timestamp":"2026-09-12T22:31:11.840Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"d7af60b9-a2bd-450d-8d80-e0f0cd6e200b","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"session-start-progressive-disclosure"}
{"type":"last-prompt","lastPrompt":"Review the conversation context below and respond with a concise summary of important items that should be preserved in the daily log. Do NOT use any tools — just return plain text.  Format your respo…","leafUuid":"02289edc-3f1c-4d2c-8649-2b62a8e61cf4","sessionId":"d7af60b9-a2bd-450d-8d80-e0f0cd6e200b"}
{"parentUuid":"02289edc-3f1c-4d2c-8649-2b62a8e61cf4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CezLYwQBJWz6eExnZ7cDG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Context:** Continuing the multi-task \"harness-agnostic AIOS\" plan (`~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-12-harness-agnostic-aios.md`, pushed as `00730b6`) — making the skills/backup stack work on both Mac and Windows. Tasks 1–2 complete; paused, then resumed at round 10 of plan review.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Codex hit its usage limit mid-gate (reset 4:46 PM). User said \"use claude, that fine\" → reviewer switched to Claude via `--host codex`, which starts a fresh review session (resume can't cross providers).\n- The Claude reviewer found what Codex missed: **14 of 19** outward symlinks in the skills repo are third-party package-manager installs (including 5 `mattpocock-skills` explicitly out of scope). Task 4 would have copied all of them into Eric's personal repo.\n- Reframed the inventory: **42 skills Eric wrote, 19 third-party links.**\n- Round-10 review findings (plan not yet approved): (1) serious — the new safety hook silently breaks the daily backup: a refused commit is ignored but still logged as \"committed\", and the blocked link stays staged so every later backup fails silently; (2) minor — text still says `.gitignore` where it should say `.git/info/exclude`; (3) minor — the Pi test user may inherit the `staff` group, stalling that boundary step.\n- User said \"pause\" (during an API ENOTFOUND error), then \"resume\".\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Third-party vendored symlinks (`claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review`) stay **out** of the `claude-skills` repo — same rule as plugins. Windows needs a separate install of that package. They were already committed and pushed as dead links on Windows; now explicit rather than silent.\n- Task 4's inversion script deleted entirely — leave the 19 third-party links alone rather than copy them in.\n- Task 2 prune executed as a **move, not delete** (reversible).\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- **`.gitignore` patterns ending in `/` match directories but NOT symlinks** — the trailing slash would have silently re-added all four dead links on the next backup run.\n- Backups must be verified by **actually restoring them** — the restore returned 57/61 skills, exposing a two-hop symlink chain (`~/.claude/skills/X → ~/.agents/skills/X → ~/.agents/vendor-review/...`) into an unbacked-up vendor folder.\n- Re-run the review gate after amending a plan — the prior approval is stale. Codex found 5 new bugs in the amendment itself.\n- `dcg` blocks `mv` with variable paths; Python with explicit containment checks is the workaround.\n- Directory counts can mismatch because `ls` omits hidden files (209 vs 208 was a hidden `.gitignore`).\n- A second reviewer with a different provider catches different classes of error — the provider switch wasn't just a fallback, it found the plan's biggest error.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Fix the three round-10 findings: make the backup report a failed commit, have the sync unstage third-party links, correct `.gitignore` → `.git/info/exclude` wording, handle the `staff`-group inheritance in the Pi boundary step.\n- Re-run the review gate, then start Tasks 3–8.\n- Windows: separately install the vendored package that provides `claudex-loop`, `claudex-route`, `codex-build`, `codex-review` (currently dead symlinks there).\n- Task 2 result to record: global skills pool pruned 306 → 208; 61 skills still resolve; ~150 third-party installs untouched."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44870,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4487